Q: Is there an inverse of System.Diagnostics.ConditionalAttribute? A: <p>This solution requires a global symbol which is guaranteed to be present.</p>
<p>Define a constant in some global file:</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public static class Constants
{

    public const string NOT_SILVERLIGHT =
#if SILVERLIGHT
        &quot;NEVER_PRESENT_SYMBOL&quot;;
#else
        &quot;ALWAYS_PRESENT_SYMBOL&quot;;
#endif
}
</code></pre>
<p>Replace <code>NEVER_PRESENT_SYMBOL</code> with a symbol that will never be present, and replace <code>ALWAYS_PRESENT_SYMBOL</code> with a symbol that will always be present (<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/preprocessor-directives#conditional-compilation" rel="nofollow noreferrer">something like NETSTANDARD and friends</a> or <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/compiler-options/language#defineconstants" rel="nofollow noreferrer">add a global symbol yourself</a>).</p>
<pre><code>[Conditional(Constants.NOT_SILVERLIGHT)]
private void DoStuffThatSilverlightCant() {...}
</code></pre>
